      "q": "A block of mass m is on an inclined plane of angle θ. The coefficient of\nfriction between the block and the plane is μ and tan θ > μ. The block is held\nstationary by applying a force P parallel to the plane. The direction of force\npointing up the plane is taken to be positive. As P is varied from P 1 =\nmg(sinθ − μ cosθ) to P 2 = mg(sinθ + μ cosθ), the frictional force f versus P\ngraph will look like\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Laws of Motion Question 28 English]",
      "qHtml": "<p>A block of mass m is on an inclined plane of angle θ. The coefficient of\nfriction between the block and the plane is μ and tan θ &gt; μ. The block is held\nstationary by applying a force P parallel to the plane. The direction of force\npointing up the plane is taken to be positive. As P is varied from P<sub>1</sub> =\nmg(sinθ − μ cosθ) to P<sub>2</sub> = mg(sinθ + μ cosθ), the frictional force f versus P\ngraph will look like</p>\n\n<img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l2y4pny3/6c18989d-795f-4d99-95d9-f36858e0868a/2109eda0-cf43-11ec-96c2-cfdd3edc6cd1/file-1l2y4pny4.png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Laws of Motion Question 28 English\" loading=\"lazy\">",
