      "s": "IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline. Correct option: A. The forces acting on the block are its weight mg, normal reaction N, applied force P and frictional force f.\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Laws of Motion Question 28 English Explanation]\n\nResolve mg along and normal to the inclined plane and apply Newton's second law to get\n\n$$0 = P + f - mg\\sin \\theta $$,\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$f = - P + mg\\sin \\theta $$. ...... (1)\n\nThis is a straight line with slope $$-$$1. Substitute the values of P 1 and P 2 in equation (1) to get the frictional force at those points i.e.,\n\n$${f_1} = \\mu mg\\cos \\theta $$ and $${f_2} = - \\mu mg\\cos \\theta $$.",
