      "q": "A bar of mass $M=1.00 \\mathrm{~kg}$ and length $L=0.20 \\mathrm{~m}$ is lying on a horizontal frictionless surface. One end of the bar is pivoted at a point about which it is free to rotate. A small mass $m=0.10 \\mathrm{~kg}$ is moving on the same horizontal surface with $5.00 \\mathrm{~m} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$ speed on a path perpendicular to the bar. It hits the bar at a distance $L / 2$ from the pivoted end and returns back on the same path with speed v. After this elastic collision, the bar rotates with an angular velocity $\\omega$.\n\nWhich of the following statement is correct?",
      "qHtml": "A bar of mass $M=1.00 \\mathrm{~kg}$ and length $L=0.20 \\mathrm{~m}$ is lying on a horizontal frictionless surface. One end of the bar is pivoted at a point about which it is free to rotate. A small mass $m=0.10 \\mathrm{~kg}$ is moving on the same horizontal surface with $5.00 \\mathrm{~m} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$ speed on a path perpendicular to the bar. It hits the bar at a distance $L / 2$ from the pivoted end and returns back on the same path with speed v. After this elastic collision, the bar rotates with an angular velocity $\\omega$. <br><br>Which of the following statement is correct?",
