      "qHtml": "Two satellites $\\mathrm{P}$ and $\\mathrm{Q}$ are moving in different circular orbits around the Earth (radius $R$ ). The heights of $\\mathrm{P}$ and $\\mathrm{Q}$ from the Earth surface are $h_{\\mathrm{P}}$ and $h_{\\mathrm{Q}}$, respectively, where $h_{\\mathrm{P}}=R / 3$. The accelerations of $\\mathrm{P}$ and $\\mathrm{Q}$ due to Earth's gravity are $g_{\\mathrm{P}}$ and $g_{\\mathrm{Q}}$, respectively. If $g_{\\mathrm{P}} / g_{\\mathrm{Q}}=36 / 25$, what is the value of $h_{\\mathrm{Q}}$ ?",
