      "q": "A planet of mass $$M,$$ has two natural satellites with masses $${m_1}$$ and $${m_2}.$$ The radii of their circular orbits are $${R_1}$$ and $${R_2}$$ respectively, Ignore the gravitational force between the satellites. Define $${v_1},{L_1},{K_1}$$ and $${T_1}$$ to be , respectively, the orbital speed, angular momentum, kinetic energy and time period of revolution of satellite $$1$$; and $${v_2},{L_2},{K_2},$$ and $${T_2}$$ to be the corresponding quantities of satellite $$2.$$ Given $${m_1}/{m_2} = 2$$ and $${R_1}/{R_2} = 1/4,$$ match the ratios in List- $${\\rm I}$$ to the numbers in List -$${\\rm II}.$$\n\nLIST - I\nLIST - II\n\nP.\nv 1 /v 2\n1.\n1/8\n\nQ.\nL 1 /L 2\n2.\n1\n\nR.\nK 1 /K 2\n3.\n2\n\nS.\nT 1 /T 2\n4.\n8",
      "qHtml": "A planet of mass $$M,$$ has two natural satellites with masses $${m_1}$$  and $${m_2}.$$  The radii of their circular orbits are   $${R_1}$$ and $${R_2}$$ respectively, Ignore the gravitational force between the satellites. Define $${v_1},{L_1},{K_1}$$ and $${T_1}$$ to be , respectively, the orbital speed, angular momentum, kinetic energy and time period of revolution of satellite $$1$$; and $${v_2},{L_2},{K_2},$$ and $${T_2}$$ to be the corresponding quantities of satellite $$2.$$  Given $${m_1}/{m_2} = 2$$ and $${R_1}/{R_2} = 1/4,$$  match the ratios in <b>List-</b>$${\\rm I}$$  to the numbers in <b>List</b>-$${\\rm II}.$$\n<br><br>\n<table>\n  <tbody><tr>\n    <th colspan=\"2\">LIST - I </th>\n    <th colspan=\"2\">LIST - II</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>P.</td>\n    <td>v<sub>1</sub>/v<sub>2</sub></td>\n    <td>1.</td>\n    <td>1/8</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Q.</td>\n    <td>L<sub>1</sub>/L<sub>2</sub></td>\n    <td>2.</td>\n    <td>1</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>R.</td>\n    <td>K<sub>1</sub>/K<sub>2</sub></td>\n    <td>3.</td>\n    <td>2</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>S.</td>\n    <td>T<sub>1</sub>/T<sub>2</sub></td>\n    <td>4.</td>\n    <td>8</td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody></table>",
