      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline. Correct option: A. For horizontal flow, Bernoulli's theorem becomes\n\n$${P \\over \\rho } + gh + {1 \\over 2}{v^2} = k'$$\n\n$$P + {1 \\over 2}\\rho {v^2} = k$$ (h = 0)\n\nBetween points 1 and 2 :\n\n$${P_1} - {P_2} = {1 \\over 2}{\\rho _a}v_a^2$$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Properties of Matter Question 25 English Explanation]\n\nBetween points 2 and 3 :\n\n$${P_3} - {P_2} = {1 \\over 2}{\\rho _l}v_l^2$$\n\nSince, P 1 = P 3 , we have\n\n$${1 \\over 2}{\\rho _l}v_l^2 = {1 \\over 2}{\\rho _a}v_a^2$$\n\n$${{{v_l}} \\over {{v_a}}} =\\sqrt {{{{\\rho _a}} \\over {{\\rho _l}}}} $$",
      "source": "JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline | Mechanical Properties of Fluids | 1l17k5crh",
      "pyq": true,
      "exactPaperText": true,
      "pyqSourceSlug": "properties-of-matter"
