      "q": "Column II gives certain systems undergoing a process. Column I suggests changes in some of the parameters related to the system. Match the statements in Column I to the appropriate process(es) from Column II:\n\nColumn I\n\nColumn II\n\n(A)\nThe energy of the system is increased.\n(P)\nSystem : A capacitor, initially uncharged.\nProcess : It is connected to a battery.\n\n(B)\nMechanical energy is provided to the system, which is converted into energy of random motion of its parts.\n(Q)\nSystem : A gas in an adiabatic container filled with an adiabatic piston.\nProcess : The gas is compressed by pushing the piston.\n\n(C)\nInternal energy of the system is converted into its mechanical energy.\n(R)\nSystem : A gas in a rigid container.\nProcess : The gas gets cooled due to colder atmosphere surrounding it.\n\n(D)\nMass of the system is decreased.\n(S)\nSystem : A heavy nucleus, initially at rest.\nProcess : The nucleus fissions into two fragments of nearly equal masses and some neutrons are emitted.\n\n(T)\nSystem : A resistive wire loop.\nProcess : The loop is placed in a time varying magnetic field perpendicular to its plane.",
