      "q": "List I describes thermodynamic processes in four different systems. List II gives the magnitudes (either exactly or as a close approximation) of possible changes in the internal energy of the system due to the process.\n\nList-I\nList-II\n\n(I) $10^{-3} \\mathrm{~kg}$ of water at $100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is converted to steam at the same temperature, at a pressure of $10^{5} \\mathrm{~Pa}$. The volume of the system changes from $10^{-6} \\mathrm{~m}^{3}$ to $10^{-3} \\mathrm{~m}^{3}$ in the process. Latent heat of water $=2250\\, \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{kg}$.\n\n(P) $2 \\mathrm{~kJ}$\n\n(II) $0.2$ moles of a rigid diatomic ideal gas with volume $V$ at temperature $500 \\mathrm{~K}$ undergoes an isobaric expansion to volume $3 \\mathrm{~V}$. Assume $R=8.0 \\mathrm{Jmol}^{-1} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1}$.\n\n(Q) $7 k J$\n\n(III) One mole of a monatomic ideal gas is compressed adiabatically from volume $V=\\frac{1}{3} \\mathrm{~m}^{3}$ and pressure $2 \\mathrm{kPa}$ to volume $\\frac{V}{8}$.\n\n(R) $4 \\mathrm{~kJ}$\n\n(IV) Three moles of a diatomic ideal gas whose molecules can vibrate, is given $9 \\mathrm{~kJ}$ of heat and undergoes isobaric expansion.\n\n(S) $5 \\mathrm{~kJ}$\n\n(T) $3 \\mathrm{~kJ}$\n\nWhich one of the following options is correct?",
      "qHtml": "<p> List I describes thermodynamic processes in four different systems. List II gives the magnitudes (either exactly or as a close approximation) of possible changes in the internal energy of the system due to the process.</p>\n<p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n  <tr>\n    <th>List-I</th>\n    <th><span>List-II</span></th>\n  </tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(I) $10^{-3} \\mathrm{~kg}$ of water at $100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is converted to steam at the same temperature, at a pressure of $10^{5} \\mathrm{~Pa}$. The volume of the system changes from $10^{-6} \\mathrm{~m}^{3}$ to $10^{-3} \\mathrm{~m}^{3}$ in the process. Latent heat of water $=2250\\, \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{kg}$.<br></td>\n    <td>(P) $2 \\mathrm{~kJ}$ </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(II) $0.2$ moles of a rigid diatomic ideal gas with volume $V$ at temperature $500 \\mathrm{~K}$ undergoes an isobaric expansion to volume $3 \\mathrm{~V}$. Assume $R=8.0 \\mathrm{Jmol}^{-1} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1}$.<br></td>\n    <td><span>(Q) $7 k J$</span></td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(III) One mole of a monatomic ideal gas is compressed adiabatically from volume $V=\\frac{1}{3} \\mathrm{~m}^{3}$ and pressure $2 \\mathrm{kPa}$ to volume $\\frac{V}{8}$.<br></td>\n    <td>(R) $4 \\mathrm{~kJ}$</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(IV) Three moles of a diatomic ideal gas whose molecules can vibrate, is given $9 \\mathrm{~kJ}$ of heat and undergoes isobaric expansion.<br></td>\n    <td>(S) $5 \\mathrm{~kJ}$</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td></td>\n    <td>(T) $3 \\mathrm{~kJ}$</td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></p>\n<p>Which one of the following options is correct?\n</p>",
