      "q": "One mole of an ideal gas expands adiabatically from an initial state $\\left(T_{\\mathrm{A}}, V_0\\right)$ to final state $\\left(T_{\\mathrm{f}}, 5 V_0\\right)$. Another mole of the same gas expands isothermally from a different initial state $\\left(T_{\\mathrm{B}}, V_0\\right)$ to the same final state $\\left(T_{\\mathrm{f}}, 5 V_0\\right)$. The ratio of the specific heats at constant pressure and constant volume of this ideal gas is $\\gamma$. What is the ratio $T_{\\mathrm{A}} / T_{\\mathrm{B}}$ ?",
      "qHtml": "One mole of an ideal gas expands adiabatically from an initial state $\\left(T_{\\mathrm{A}}, V_0\\right)$ to final state $\\left(T_{\\mathrm{f}}, 5 V_0\\right)$. Another mole of the same gas expands isothermally from a different initial state $\\left(T_{\\mathrm{B}}, V_0\\right)$ to the same final state $\\left(T_{\\mathrm{f}}, 5 V_0\\right)$. The ratio of the specific heats at constant pressure and constant volume of this ideal gas is $\\gamma$. What is the ratio $T_{\\mathrm{A}} / T_{\\mathrm{B}}$ ?",
