      "q": "An electric dipole is formed by two charges $+q$ and $-q$ located in $x y$-plane at $(0,2) \\mathrm{mm}$ and $(0,-2) \\mathrm{mm}$, respectively, as shown in the figure. The electric potential at point $P(100,100) \\mathrm{mm}$ due to the dipole is $V_0$. The charges $+q$ and $-q$ are then moved to the points $(-1,2) \\mathrm{mm}$ and $(1,-2) \\mathrm{mm}$, respectively. What is the value of electric potential at $P$ due to the new dipole?\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2023 Paper 2 Online Physics - Electrostatics Question 12 English]",
      "qHtml": "An electric dipole is formed by two charges $+q$ and $-q$ located in $x y$-plane at $(0,2) \\mathrm{mm}$ and $(0,-2) \\mathrm{mm}$, respectively, as shown in the figure. The electric potential at point $P(100,100) \\mathrm{mm}$ due to the dipole is $V_0$. The charges $+q$ and $-q$ are then moved to the points $(-1,2) \\mathrm{mm}$ and $(1,-2) \\mathrm{mm}$, respectively. What is the value of electric potential at $P$ due to the new dipole?\n<br><br><img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1liioyoet/096d05dc-e5c2-4eda-a14b-9724c8e696b4/3def7450-0389-11ee-add3-0f52d4fe427d/file-1liioyoeu.png\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2023 Paper 2 Online Physics - Electrostatics Question 12 English\" loading=\"lazy\">",
