      "s": "IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 2 Offline. Correct option: B. When cavity is not present:\n\nElectric field inside the solid sphere\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}_{1}}=\\frac{\\rho}{3 \\varepsilon_{0}} \\overrightarrow{r_{1}}\n$$ ..... (i)\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Electrostatics Question 15 English Explanation 1]\n\nSolid sphere after making cavity inside solid sphere,\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Electrostatics Question 15 English Explanation 2]\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}_{2}}=\\frac{\\rho}{3 \\varepsilon_{0}} \\overrightarrow{r_{2}}\n$$ ...... (ii)\n\n$${\\overrightarrow E _{net}} = \\overrightarrow {{E_1}} - \\overrightarrow {{E_2}} = {\\rho \\over {3{\\varepsilon _0}}}\\overrightarrow {{r_1}} - {\\rho \\over {3{\\varepsilon _0}}}\\overrightarrow {{r_2}} $$\n\n$$=\\frac{\\rho}{3 \\varepsilon_{0}}\\left(\\overrightarrow{r_{1}}-\\overrightarrow{r_{2}}\\right)\n$$ ...... (iii)\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Electrostatics Question 15 English Explanation 3]\n\nFrom eq (iii), we get\n\n$$\\therefore \\quad \\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{net}}=\\frac{\\rho}{3 \\varepsilon_{0}}(\\vec{r})$$\n\nHence, electric field inside the emptied space (cavity) is non-zero and uniform.",
