      "q": "List-I shows four configurations, each consisting of a pair of ideal electric dipoles. Each dipole has a dipole moment of magnitude $p$, oriented as marked by arrows in the figures. In all the configurations the dipoles are fixed such that they are at a distance $2 r$ apart along the $x$ direction. The midpoint of the line joining the two dipoles is $X$. The possible resultant electric fields $\\vec{E}$ at $X$ are given in List-II.\n\nChoose the option that describes the correct match between the entries in List-I to those in List-II .\n\nList–I\n\nList–II\n\n(P)\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2025 Paper 1 Online Physics - Electrostatics Question 4 English 1]\n\n(1) $$\n\\vec{E}=0\n$$\n\n(Q)\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2025 Paper 1 Online Physics - Electrostatics Question 4 English 2]\n\n(2) $\\displaystyle \\vec{E} = -\\,\\frac{p}{2\\pi\\epsilon_0\\,r^3}\\,\\hat{\\jmath}$\n\n(R)\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2025 Paper 1 Online Physics - Electrostatics Question 4 English 3]\n\n(3) $\\displaystyle \\vec{E} = -\\,\\frac{p}{4\\pi\\epsilon_0\\,r^3}\\,(\\hat{\\imath} - \\hat{\\jmath})$\n\n(S)\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2025 Paper 1 Online Physics - Electrostatics Question 4 English 4]\n\n(4) $\\displaystyle \\vec{E} = \\frac{p}{4\\pi\\epsilon_0\\,r^3}\\,(2\\hat{\\imath} - \\hat{\\jmath})$\n\n(5) $\\displaystyle \\vec{E} = \\frac{p}{\\pi\\epsilon_0\\,r^3}\\,\\hat{\\imath}$",
      "qHtml": "<p>List-I shows four configurations, each consisting of a pair of ideal electric dipoles. Each dipole has a dipole moment of magnitude $p$, oriented as marked by arrows in the figures. In all the configurations the dipoles are fixed such that they are at a distance $2 r$ apart along the $x$ direction. The midpoint of the line joining the two dipoles is $X$. The possible resultant electric fields $\\vec{E}$ at $X$ are given in List-II.</p>\n<p>Choose the option that describes the correct match between the entries in <b>List-I</b> to those in <b>List-II</b>.</p>\n<table>\n\n  <tbody><tr>\n\n    <th>List–I</th>\n\n    <th>List–II</th>\n\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n\n    <td>(P) <img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1mb0e2pjn/74071b78-dfe9-4def-be31-55e7cbfe0c6e/d3ed2230-379a-11f0-831e-111c9abd7f64/file-jaoe38c1mb0e2pjo.png\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2025 Paper 1 Online Physics - Electrostatics Question 4 English 1\" loading=\"lazy\"></td>\n\n    <td>(1) $$\n\\vec{E}=0\n$$</td>\n\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n\n    <td>(Q) <img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1mb0e2wnd/f8337145-2fe4-410f-aac3-728c55e68de7/d969db90-379a-11f0-831e-111c9abd7f64/file-jaoe38c1mb0e2wne.png\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2025 Paper 1 Online Physics - Electrostatics Question 4 English 2\" loading=\"lazy\"></td>\n\n    <td>(2) $\\displaystyle \\vec{E} = -\\,\\frac{p}{2\\pi\\epsilon_0\\,r^3}\\,\\hat{\\jmath}$</td>\n\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n\n    <td>(R) <img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1mb0e317f/ae1b25f5-dda8-4f06-8478-7d286fbd7efb/dcef0ab0-379a-11f0-831e-111c9abd7f64/file-jaoe38c1mb0e317g.png\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2025 Paper 1 Online Physics - Electrostatics Question 4 English 3\" loading=\"lazy\"></td>\n\n    <td>(3) $\\displaystyle \\vec{E} = -\\,\\frac{p}{4\\pi\\epsilon_0\\,r^3}\\,(\\hat{\\imath} - \\hat{\\jmath})$</td>\n\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n\n    <td>(S) <img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1mb0e3588/9f8636fc-807c-4eb0-a18b-091460276283/e00a7b80-379a-11f0-831e-111c9abd7f64/file-jaoe38c1mb0e3589.png\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2025 Paper 1 Online Physics - Electrostatics Question 4 English 4\" loading=\"lazy\"></td>\n\n    <td>(4) $\\displaystyle \\vec{E} = \\frac{p}{4\\pi\\epsilon_0\\,r^3}\\,(2\\hat{\\imath} - \\hat{\\jmath})$</td>\n\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n\n    <td></td>\n\n    <td>(5) $\\displaystyle \\vec{E} = \\frac{p}{\\pi\\epsilon_0\\,r^3}\\,\\hat{\\imath}$</td>\n\n  </tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
