      "a": 2,
      "s": "IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline. Correct option: C. To verify Ohm's law, we need to measure the voltage across the test resistance R T and current passing through it. The voltage can be measured by connecting a high resistance R 1 in series with galvanometer. This combination becomes a voltmeter and should be connected in parallel to R T . The current can be measured by connecting a low resistance R 2 (shunt) in parallel with galvanometer. This combination becomes an ammeter and should be connected in series to measure the current through R T .",
