      "q": "You are given many resistances, capacitors and inductors. These are connected to a variable DC voltage source (the first two circuits) or an AC voltage source of 50 Hz frequency (the next three circuits) in different ways as shown in Column II. When a current I (steady state for DC or rms for AC) flows through the circuit, the corresponding voltage $V_1$ and $V_2$ (indicated in circuits) are related as shown in Column I. Match the two :\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Alternating Current Question 5 English 1]\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Alternating Current Question 5 English 2]",
      "qHtml": "<p>You are given many resistances, capacitors and inductors. These are connected to a variable DC voltage source (the first two circuits) or an AC voltage source of 50 Hz frequency (the next three circuits) in different ways as shown in Column II. When a current I (steady state for DC or rms for AC) flows through the circuit, the corresponding voltage $V_1$ and $V_2$ (indicated in circuits) are related as shown in Column I. Match the two :</p>\n\n<img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1m4mc4eqp/f66d0fa5-b86c-46fc-ac1d-2cbfd1dcb5f2/eb934110-b916-11ef-bcaa-6bb34cbe24da/file-jaoe38c1m4mc4eqq.png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Alternating Current Question 5 English 1\" loading=\"lazy\">\n\n<img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1m4mc5l3e/14e8bfb9-363b-49f2-9fee-c6e8703f3b84/0c4aa6a0-b917-11ef-bcaa-6bb34cbe24da/file-jaoe38c1m4mc5l3f.png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Alternating Current Question 5 English 2\" loading=\"lazy\">",
