      "s": "JEE Advanced 2024 Paper 1 Online. Correct option: A. [Diagram: JEE Advanced 2024 Paper 1 Online Physics - Alternating Current Question 6 English Explanation 1]\n\n(P) When $$K_1$$ is closed current in $$R_0$$ is $$I_1$$\n\nAt $$\\mathrm{t}=0$$; circuit will be\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2024 Paper 1 Online Physics - Alternating Current Question 6 English Explanation 2]\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{I}_1=0 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{P} \\rightarrow(1)\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\n(Q) After long time inductor behave as a wire so $$I_2$$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2024 Paper 1 Online Physics - Alternating Current Question 6 English Explanation 3]\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{I}_2=\\frac{20}{5}=4 \\mathrm{~A} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Q} \\rightarrow(3)\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\n$$\\text { (R) When } K_2 \\text { is closed and } K_1 \\text { open }$$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2024 Paper 1 Online Physics - Alternating Current Question 6 English Explanation 4]\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\omega_0=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\mathrm{LC}}} \\\\\n& \\omega_0=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{25 \\times 10^{-3} \\times 10 \\times 10^{-6}}}=\\frac{1}{5 \\times 10^{-4}} \\\\\n& \\omega_0=2 \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s} \\\\\n& \\omega_0=2 \\mathrm{kilo}-\\mathrm{radian} / \\mathrm{s} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{R} \\rightarrow(2)\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\n(S) Now $$K_2$$ is closed and $$K_1$$ open\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2024 Paper 1 Online Physics - Alternating Current Question 6 English Explanation 5]\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{LI}_2^2=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{CV}_0^2 \\\\\n& 25 \\times 10^{-3} \\times(4)^2=10 \\times 10^{-6} \\times \\mathrm{V}_0^2 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~V}_0^2=2500 \\times 16 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~V}_0=50 \\times 4=200 \\mathrm{~V} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~S} \\rightarrow(5)\n\\end{aligned}$$",
