      "qHtml": "<p>STATEMENT 1</p>\n<p>A vertical iron rod has a coil of wire wound over it at the bottom end. An alternating current flows in the coil. The rod goes through a conducting ring as shown in the figure. The ring can float at a certain height above the coil.</p>\n<p><img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lguf416o/118a7b5f-ef17-4f37-80ed-c3cf385ecd8c/b097a000-e263-11ed-8ec0-d5a0bb2b1e44/file-1lguf416p.png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Alternating Current Question 8 English\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>\n<p>Because</p>\n<p>STATEMENT 2</p>\n<p>In the above situation, a current is induced in the ring which interacts with the horizontal component of the magnetic field to produce an average force in the upward direction.</p>",
