      "s": "IIT-JEE 2005 Mains. Correct option: D. If $$c_{1}$$ be the critical angle for the interface AB in figure.\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rlr}\nn_{2} \\sin c_{1} & =n_{1} \\sin 90^{\\circ} & \\left(n_{1}=\\sqrt{2}\\right. \\\\\n2 \\sin c_{1} & =\\sqrt{2} \\times 1 & \\left.n_{2}=2\\right) \\\\\n\\sin c_{1} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\sin 45^{\\circ} \\\\\nc_{1} & =45^{\\circ} \\\\\nn_{1} & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\\nn_{2} & =2 \\\\\n\\hline n_{3} & =\\sqrt{3}\n\\end{array}$$\n\nSince, AB and CD are parallel, the angle of\nincidence for both will be equal.\n\nIf $$c_{2}$$ be the critical angle for the interface CD.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\nn_{2} \\sin c_{2} & =n_{3} \\sin 90^{\\circ} \\quad\\left(n_{3}=\\sqrt{3}\\right) \\\\\n2 \\sin c_{2} & =\\sqrt{3} \\times 1 \\\\\n\\sin c_{2} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}=\\sin 60^{\\circ} \\\\\nc_{2} & =60^{\\circ}\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe minimum value of the angle of incidence must be equal to the greater of the values of $$c_{1}$$ and $$c_{2}$$.\n\n$$\\therefore$$ Minimum angle of incidence is $$60^{\\circ}$$.",
