      "q": "A biconvex lens is formed with two planoconvex lenses as shown in the figure. Refractive index n of the first lens is 1.5 and that of the second lens is 1.2. Both curved surface are of the same radius of curvature R = 14 cm. For this biconvex lens, for an object distance of 40 cm, the image distance will be\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Geometrical Optics Question 42 English]",
      "qHtml": "<p>A biconvex lens is formed with two planoconvex lenses as shown in the figure. Refractive index n of the first lens is 1.5 and that of the second lens is 1.2. Both curved surface are of the same radius of curvature R = 14 cm. For this biconvex lens, for an object distance of 40 cm, the image distance will be</p>\n<p><img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l24kme2r/3543bbc8-fe94-464b-aa5c-5439681b1539/d4921a20-bf01-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24kme2s.png\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Geometrical Optics Question 42 English\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>",
