      "s": "JEE Advanced 2022 Paper 2 Online. Correct option: A. By Einstein's photoelectric equation, we have:\n\n$\n\n\\mathrm{KE} =h v-\\phi$\n\n$\nh v-\\phi =6 \\mathrm{eV} $\n\n$\n\\frac{h c}{\\lambda}-\\phi =6 \\mathrm{eV} $ .........(i)\n\n$\n\\frac{h c}{4 \\lambda}-\\phi =0.6 \\mathrm{eV} $\n\n$\n\\frac{3 h c}{4 \\lambda} =5.4 \\mathrm{eV}$\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow $$ $\\lambda=\\frac{3 h c}{5.4 \\mathrm{eV} \\times 4} $\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow $$ $\n\\lambda =\\frac{3 \\times 1.24 \\times 10^{-6}}{4 \\times 5.4}=1.72 \\times \\times^{-7} \\mathrm{~m}$ ........(ii)\n\nFrom equation (i) and (ii), we conclude\n\n$\\frac{h c}{1.72 \\times 10^{-7}} \\times \\frac{1}{1.6 \\times 10^{-19}}-\\phi=6 \\mathrm{eV}$\n\non subsituting all the values we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\phi=(7.27-6) \\\\\\\\\n&\\Rightarrow \\phi=1.27 \\mathrm{eV} \\\\\\\\\n&\\Rightarrow \\phi=1.20 \\mathrm{eV}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
