      "a": 2,
      "s": "IIT-JEE 2005 Mains. Correct option: C. 1 division of main scale = 1 mm\n\nNumber of division in vernier scale = 10\n\nMass of cube = 2.736 g\n\nLeast count of vernier callipers = (1 main scale\ndivision) $$-$$ (1 vernier scale division)\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n& =1 \\mathrm{~mm}-\\frac{9}{10} \\mathrm{~mm} \\\\\n& =1 \\mathrm{~mm}-0.9 \\mathrm{~mm} \\\\\n& =0.1 \\mathrm{~mm}\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nLength of the cube as measured by vernier\ncallipers\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n& =10 \\mathrm{~mm}+(1 \\times 0.1 \\mathrm{~mm}) \\\\\n& =10 \\mathrm{~mm}+0.1 \\mathrm{~mm} \\\\\n& =10.1 \\mathrm{~mm} \\\\\n& =1.01 \\mathrm{~cm}\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\ndensity of the material of the cube $$=\\frac{\\text { mass }}{\\text { volume }}$$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\rho & =\\frac{2.736 \\mathrm{~g}}{(1.01)^{3} \\mathrm{~cm}^{3}} \\\\\n& =2.66 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{cm}^{3} \\\\\n\\rho \\text { in SI } & =2.66 \\times 10^{3} \\mathrm{~kg} / \\mathrm{m}^{3} .\n\\end{aligned}$$",
