      "s": "JEE Advanced 2023 Paper 2 Online. Correct option: C. (1) Upto 14 electrons, molecular orbital configuration is ->\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2023 Paper 2 Online Chemistry - Chemical Bonding & Molecular Structure Question 10 English Explanation 1]\n\nN b = No of electrons in bonding molecular orbital\n\nN a $$=$$ No of electrons in anti bonding molecular orbital\n\nHere N a = Anti bonding electron $$=$$ 4 and N b = 10\n\n(2) After 14 electrons to 20 electrons molecular orbital configuration is ->\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2023 Paper 2 Online Chemistry - Chemical Bonding & Molecular Structure Question 10 English Explanation 2]\n\nHere N a = 10\n\nand N b = 10\n\nNow from question, in F atom 9 electrons present, so in F 2 , 9 $$ \\times $$ 2 = 18 electrons present.\n\nMolecular orbital configuration of F 2 (18 electrons) is\n\n$${\\sigma _{1{s^2}}}\\,\\sigma _{1{s^2}}^ * \\,{\\sigma _{2{s^2}}}\\,\\sigma _{2{s^2}}^ * \\,{\\sigma _{2p_z^2}}\\,{\\pi _{2p_x^2}}\\, = \\,{\\pi _{2p_y^2}}\\,\\pi _{2p_x^2}^ * \\, = \\,\\pi _{2p_y^2}^ * $$",
