      "q": "The standard enthalpies of formation of CO 2 (g), H 2 O(l) and glucose(s) at 25 o C are –400 kJ/mol,\n–300 kJ/mol and –1300 kJ/mol, respectively. The standard enthalpy of combustion per gram of glucose at\n25 o C is",
      "qHtml": "The standard enthalpies of formation of CO<sub>2</sub>(g), H<sub>2</sub>O(l) and glucose(s) at 25<sup>o</sup>C are –400 kJ/mol,\n–300 kJ/mol and –1300 kJ/mol, respectively. The standard enthalpy of combustion per gram of glucose at\n25<sup>o</sup>C is",
