      "s": "JEE Advanced 2025 Paper 1 Online. Correct option: B. Reaction of permanganate ion with iodide ion in neutral aqueous medium\n\nIn neutral medium, $\\mathrm{MnO}_4^{-}$is reduced to $\\mathrm{MnO}_2$ and io did ion oxidizes to $\\mathrm{IO}_3^{-}$.\n\nIn the reaction of $\\mathrm{MnO}_4^{-}$and $I^{-}, \\mathrm{MnO}_4^{-}$is the oxidizing agent (it gets reduced) and $I^{-}$acts as the reducing agent (it get oxidized).\n\nThe products of the redux reaction between $\\mathrm{MnO}_4^{-1}$ and $I^{-}$is determined by the reaction medium.\n\nIn acidic medium, $\\mathrm{MnO}_4^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Mn}^{2+}$\n\nIn basic medium, $\\mathrm{MnO}_4^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{MnO}_4^{2-}$\n\nIn neutral medium, $\\mathrm{MnO}_4^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{MnO}_2$\n\nHere, the reaction medium given is neutral and hence $\\mathrm{MnO}_4^{-}$is reduced to $\\mathrm{MnO}_2$.\nAlso, the $\\mathrm{I}^{-}$ion is oxidized to $\\mathrm{IO}_3^{-}$in the neutral medium.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{MnO}_4^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{MnO}_2 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{I}^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{IO}_3^{-}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe balanced chemical equation can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{2MnO}_4^{-}+\\mathrm{I}^{-}+\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{IMnO}_2+\\mathrm{IO}_3^{-}+2 \\mathrm{OH}^{-}\n$$\n\nAnswer: Option (B) $\\mathrm{IO}_3^{-}$",
