      "a": 2,
      "s": "JEE Advanced 2017 Paper 2 Offline. Correct option: C. Let oxidation states of phosphorus in H 3 PO 2 , H 3 PO 4 , H 3 PO 3 and H 4 P 2 O 6 be p, q, r and s respectively.\n\nOxidation state of hydrogen = + 1\n\nOxidation state of oxygen = $$-$$2\n\nThus, in H 3 PO 2 :\n\n3 $$\\times$$ (+1) + p + 2 $$\\times$$ ($$-$$2) = 0 $$\\therefore$$ p = +1\n\nIn H 3 PO 4 :\n\n3 $$\\times$$ (+1) + q + 4 $$\\times$$ ($$-$$2) = 0 $$\\therefore$$ q = +5\n\nIn H 3 PO 3 :\n\n3 $$\\times$$ (+1) + r + 3 $$\\times$$ ($$-$$2) = 0 $$\\therefore$$ r = + 3\n\nIn H 4 P 2 O 6 :\n\n4 $$\\times$$ (+1) + 2s + 6 $$\\times$$ ($$-$$2) = 0 $$\\therefore$$ s = +4\n\nThus, the order of oxidation state is :\n\nH 3 PO 4 > H 4 P 2 O 6 > H 3 PO 3 > H 3 PO 2",
      "source": "JEE Advanced 2017 Paper 2 Offline | Redox Reactions | xnwnMZXX4E0z3ldn",
