      "q": "The Fischer projection of D-erythrose is shown below :\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2020 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 36 English 1]\n\nD-erythrose and its isomers are listed as P, Q, R, and S in Column - I. Choose the correct relationship of P, Q, R, and S with D-erythrose from Column - II.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2020 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 36 English 2]",
      "qHtml": "The Fischer projection of D-erythrose is shown below :<br><br> <img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ks56w904/4d57ab6c-f1f7-4007-9e4a-c1fd6a8dddfc/c5cbc540-f95e-11eb-896d-4d830e0f8af0/file-1ks56w905.jpeg\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2020 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 36 English 1\" loading=\"lazy\"> <br><br>D-erythrose and its isomers are listed as P, Q, R, and S in Column - I. Choose the correct relationship of P, Q, R, and S with D-erythrose from Column - II.\n<br> <img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ks56y7sd/4531f690-40b7-49ca-9454-23257e93d79f/fc79b9d0-f95e-11eb-a269-21f97bcfdc63/file-1ks56y7se.jpeg\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2020 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 36 English 2\" loading=\"lazy\">",
