      "a": 0,
      "s": "IIT-JEE 2005 Screening. Correct option: A. We know, for ionic compounds, elevation in boiling point $$\\Delta$$T b = k b $$\\times$$ molality (m) $$\\times$$ i\n\nGiven, k b = 0.52 K molal $$-$$1\n\nNow, molality (m) = $${{mass\\,of\\,solute \\div molar\\,mass} \\over {mass\\,of\\,solvent}} \\times 1000$$\n\nor, $$m = {{13.44/134.4} \\over {1000}} \\times 1000 = 0.1$$ mol kg $$-$$1\n\nWe know, $$\\alpha = {{i - 1} \\over {n - 1}}$$\n\nNow, 1 molecule of CuCl 2 on dissociation in solution produces 3 ions\n\nCuCl 2 (aq) $$\\to$$ Cu 2+ (aq) + 2Cl $$-$$ (aq)\n\nHence, n = 3\n\nIf it is assumed that CuCl 2 undergoes complete dissociation in solution, then $$\\alpha$$ = 1\n\n$$\\therefore$$ $$1 = {{i - 1} \\over {3 - 1}}$$ or, i = 3\n\nFor a solution of an electrolyte, $$\\Delta$$T b = i $$\\times$$ k b $$\\times$$ m\n\n$$\\therefore$$ $$\\Delta$$T b = 3 $$\\times$$ 0.52 $$\\times$$ 0.1 = 0.156 K\n\n$$\\therefore$$ Elevation of boiling point of the solution = 0.156 K",
      "source": "IIT-JEE 2005 Screening | Solutions | YqxnJ22JuCm12QsN",
