      "q": "The standard reduction potential data at 25 o C is given below:\n\nE o (Fe 3+ , Fe 2+ ) = +0.77V;\n\nE o (Fe 2+ , Fe) = -0.44V;\n\nE o (Cu 2+ , Cu) = +0.34V;\n\nE o (Cu + , Cu) = +0.52V;\n\nE o [O 2 (g) + 4H + + 4e - $$\\to$$ 2H 2 O] = +1.23V;\n\nE o [O 2 (g) + 2H 2 O + 4e - $$\\to$$ 4OH - ] = +0.40 V\n\nE o (Cr 3+ , Cr) = -0.74V;\n\nE o (Cr 2+ , Cr) = -0.91V;\n\nMatch E o of the redox pair in List – I with the values given in List – II and select the correct answer using\nthe code given below the lists:\n\nList - I\n\nP. E o (Fe 3+ , Fe)\n\nQ. E o (4H 2 O $$\\leftrightharpoons$$ 4H + + 4OH - )\n\nR. E o (Cu 2+ + Cu $$\\to$$ 2Cu + )\n\nS. E o (Cr 3+ , Cr 2+ )\n\nList - II\n\n1. -0.18 V\n\n2. -0.4 V\n\n3. -0.04 V\n\n4. -0.83 V",
      "qHtml": "The standard reduction potential data at 25<sup>o</sup>C is given below:<br>\nE<sup>o</sup> (Fe<sup>3+</sup> , Fe<sup>2+</sup>) = +0.77V; <br>\nE<sup>o</sup> (Fe<sup>2+</sup> , Fe) = -0.44V; <br>\nE<sup>o</sup> (Cu<sup>2+</sup> , Cu) = +0.34V; <br>\nE<sup>o</sup> (Cu<sup>+</sup> , Cu) = +0.52V; <br>\nE<sup>o</sup> [O<sub>2</sub>(g) + 4H<sup>+</sup> + 4e<sup>-</sup> $$\\to$$ 2H<sub>2</sub>O] = +1.23V; <br>\nE<sup>o</sup> [O<sub>2</sub>(g) + 2H<sub>2</sub>O + 4e<sup>-</sup> $$\\to$$ 4OH<sup>-</sup>] = +0.40 V<br>\nE<sup>o</sup> (Cr<sup>3+</sup> , Cr) = -0.74V; <br>\nE<sup>o</sup> (Cr<sup>2+</sup> , Cr) = -0.91V; <br><br>\nMatch E<sup>o</sup> of the redox pair in List – I with the values given in List – II and select the correct answer using\nthe code given below the lists:\n<br><br>\n<b>List - I</b><br>\nP. E<sup>o</sup> (Fe<sup>3+</sup> , Fe)<br>\nQ. E<sup>o</sup> (4H<sub>2</sub>O $$\\leftrightharpoons$$ 4H<sup>+</sup> + 4OH<sup>-</sup>)<br>\nR. E<sup>o</sup> (Cu<sup>2+</sup>  + Cu $$\\to$$ 2Cu<sup>+</sup>)<br>\nS. E<sup>o</sup> (Cr<sup>3+</sup>, Cr<sup>2+</sup>)<br>\n<br>\n<b>List - II</b><br>\n1. -0.18 V<br>\n2. -0.4 V<br>\n3. -0.04 V<br>\n4. -0.83 V",
