      "s": "JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline. Correct option: B. The bulky groups cause steric hindrance in the formation of transition state. Therefore, higher homologues (Q) are less reactive than lower homologues (P). In compound (S), the transition state is highly stabilized by Ph-(C=O)- group, so it has highest rate of reaction towards S N 2.\n\nThe relative reactivities towards S N 2 reaction S > P > R > Q.",
