      "s": "IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline. Correct option: D. Stability of the following species depends upon the no. of $$\\alpha$$ hydrogen which can undergoes hyperconjugation as well as resonance. Higher the no. of $$\\alpha$$ hydrogen, higher will be the stability of the carbocation.\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 5 English Explanation 1]\n\nStabilizes by resonance and have six $$\\alpha$$-hydrogen atoms (hyperconjugation).\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 5 English Explanation 2]\n\nStabilizes by resonance and have three $$\\alpha$$-hydrogen atoms.\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 5 English Explanation 3]\n\nIt have five $$\\alpha$$-hydrogen atoms.\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 5 English Explanation 4]\n\nIt have only two $$\\alpha$$-hydrogen atoms.\n\n$$\\therefore$$ (I) > (III) > (II) > (IV)",
