      "a": 1,
      "s": "IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline. Correct option: B. (A)\n\nThe compound undergoes an intramolecular aldol condensation reaction in the presence of aqueous NaOH.\n\nSteps Involved :\n\nAbstraction of Proton :\n\nThe proton attached to the alpha carbon is abstracted, generating a carbanion.\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 19 English Explanation 1]\n\nNucleophilic Addition :\n\nThe carbanion attacks the electropositive carbonyl carbon, forming a cyclic intermediate.\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 19 English Explanation 2]\n\nDehydration :\n\nThe cyclic intermediate undergoes dehydration to yield the final product.\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 19 English Explanation 3]\n\nOption (A) in Column I matches with (R), (S), and (T) in Column II.\n\n(B)\n\nNucleophilic Addition :\n\nThe ketone reacts with methyl magnesium bromide, forming a secondary alcohol. This is a nucleophilic addition reaction.\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 19 English Explanation 4]\n\nNucleophilic Substitution :\n\nThe highly nucleophilic oxygen attacks the C_1 carbon of the alkyl chain from the back, displacing chlorine to form the final product.\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 19 English Explanation 5]\n\nOption (B) in Column I matches with (P) and (S) in Column II.\n\n(C)\n\nNucleophilic Addition :\n\nThe compound undergoes a nucleophilic addition reaction in the presence of $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{SO}_4$.\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 19 English Explanation 6]\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 19 English Explanation 7]\n\nDehydration :\n\nThe molecule loses water, forming an alkene.\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 19 English Explanation 8]\n\nOption (C) in Column I matches with (R) and (S) in Column II.\n\n(D)\n\nThe compound reacts with sulfuric acid to form a carbocation, which undergoes electrophilic substitution.\n\nReaction :\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 19 English Explanation 9]\n\nOption (D) in Column I matches with (Q) and (R) in Column II.",
