      "s": "JEE Advanced 2017 Paper 2 Offline. Correct option: C. (d) : Greater the electron density on nitrogen, more basic is the compound. Thus, order of basicity is :\n\nIV > I > II > III\n\nThe conjugate acid of IV is stabilized by resonance with lone pairs on both $$\\ddot N{H_2}$$ groups.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2017 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 38 English Explanation 1]\n\nThe conjugate acid of I is stabilized by resonance with lone pair on $$-$$$$\\ddot N{H_2}$$ group and by hyperconjugation of $$-$$CH 3 group.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2017 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 38 English Explanation 2]\n\nThe conjugate acid of II is stabilized by resonance with lone pair on\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2017 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 38 English Explanation 3]\n\ngroup.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2017 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 38 English Explanation 4]\n\nIn compound III, the lone pair of nitrogen is involved in aromaticity. So, it is least basic.",
