      "s": "JEE Advanced 2023 Paper 1 Online. Correct option: D. 1.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& {\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}\\right)_6\\right]^{2+}} \\\\\\\\\n& \\mathrm{Fe}(26) \\longrightarrow 3 \\mathrm{~d}^6 4 \\mathrm{~s}^2 \\\\\\\\\n& \\mathrm{Fe}^{2+} \\longrightarrow 3 \\mathrm{~d}^6, \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O} \\text { is a weak field ligand. }\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the pairing does not take place.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2023 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 14 English Explanation 1]\n\n2.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& {\\left[\\mathrm{Mn}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}\\right)_6\\right]^{2+}} \\\\\\\\\n& \\mathrm{Mn}(25) \\longrightarrow 3 \\mathrm{~d}^5 4 \\mathrm{~s}^2 \\\\\\\\\n& \\mathrm{Mn}^{2+} \\longrightarrow 3 \\mathrm{~d}^5, \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O} \\text { is a weak field ligand. }\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the pairing does not take place.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2023 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 14 English Explanation 2]\n\n3.\n\n$\\left[\\mathrm{CO}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_6\\right]^{3+}$\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{CO}^{3+} \\longrightarrow[\\mathrm{Ar}] 3 \\mathrm{~d}^6\n$$\n\n$\\mathrm{NH}_3$ is a strong field ligand. So, the pairing takes place.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2023 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 14 English Explanation 3]\n\n4.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\begin{aligned}\n{\\left[\\mathrm{FeCl}_4\\right]^{-} }\n\\end{aligned} \\\\\\\\\n& x+4(-1)=-1 \\\\\\\\\n& x=+3 \\\\\\\\\n& \\mathrm{Fe}(26) \\longrightarrow 3 \\mathrm{~d}^6 4 \\mathrm{~s}^2 \\\\\\\\\n& \\mathrm{Fe}^{+3} \\longrightarrow[\\mathrm{Ar}] 3 \\mathrm{~d}^5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\mathrm{FeCl}_4$ is tetrahedral complex.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2023 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 14 English Explanation 4]\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\text { 5. }\\left[\\mathrm{COCl}_4\\right]^{2-} \\\\\\\\ & \\mathrm{CO} \\longrightarrow 3 \\mathrm{~d}^7 4 \\mathrm{~s}^2 \\\\\\\\ & \\mathrm{CO}^{2+} \\longrightarrow 3 \\mathrm{~d}^7 \\end{aligned}$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2023 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 14 English Explanation 5]\n\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{P} \\rightarrow 3, \\mathrm{Q} \\rightarrow 2, \\mathrm{R} \\rightarrow 4, \\mathrm{~S} \\rightarrow 1$",
