      "s": "JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline. Correct option: B. The electronic configurations of the central metal ions are as follows:\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 36 English Explanation 1]\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 36 English Explanation 2]\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 36 English Explanation 3]\n\nThe number of unpaired electrons is P = 5, Q = 3 and R = 4. From the relation $$\\mu = \\sqrt {n(n + 2)} $$, where n is the number of unpaired electrons, we have the order of spin only magnetic moment as Q < R < P.",
