      "s": "IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline. Correct option: B. In [Ni(CO)$$_4$$], Ni is in 0 oxidation state, so there are 8 electrons in 3d subshell and 2 electrons in 4s. CO is the strong ligand, so it cause pairing of electrons in 3d subshell leaving one d subshell vacant. Now, the electron from s shell shifts to d creating vacant space in s subshell and thus the hybridisation is sp$$^3$$.\n\nNi(28) = [Ar] 4s$$^2$$3d$$^8$$\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 21 English Explanation 1]\n\nCO is a strong ligand, causes coupling.\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 21 English Explanation 2]\n\nIn [Ni(CN)$$_4$$]$$^{2-}$$, Ni is in +2 oxidation state so it has 8 electrons in d subshell and CN is also a strong ligand which pairs with d subshell atom and leaves one d orbital empty and thus its hybridisation is dsp$$^2$$.\n\nIn [Ni(CN)$$_4$$]$$^{2-}$$, the oxidation state of Ni is +2\n\nNi$$^{2+}$$ = [Ar] 3d$$^8$$4s$$^0$$\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 21 English Explanation 3]\n\nCN$$^-$$ is strong ligand, causes coupling.\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 21 English Explanation 4]",
