      "s": "JEE Advanced 2021 Paper 1 Online. Correct option: A. $${[Cr{(N{H_3})_6}]^{3 + }}$$\n\nAtomic number of Cr = 24\n\nElectron configuration of Cr = 1s 2 2s 2 2p 6 3s 2 3p 6 3d 5 4s 1\n\nElectronic configuration of Cr 3+ = 1s 2 2s 2 2p 6 3s 2 3p 6 3d 3 4s 0\n\nNH 3 is a weak field ligand. The splitting of d-orbital occur.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2021 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 45 English Explanation 1]\n\nNumber of unpaired electrons, n = 3\n\nMagnetic moment (spin only), $${\\mu _s} = \\sqrt {n(n + 2)} BM$$\n\n$$ = \\sqrt {3(3 + 2)} = \\sqrt {3 \\times 5} = \\sqrt {15} = 3.87BM$$\n\n$${[Cu{F_6}]^{3 - }}$$ Atomic number of Cu = 29\n\nElectronic configuration of Cu = 1s 2 2s 2 2p 6 3s 2 3p 6 3d 10 4s 1\n\nElectronic configuration of Cu 2+ = 1s 2 2s 2 2p 6 3s 2 3p 6 3d 8 4s 0\n\nF $$-$$ is a weak field ligand, so splitting of d-orbitals occur as follows:\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2021 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 45 English Explanation 2]\n\nNumber of unpaired electrons, n = 2\n\nSpin only magnetic moment, $${\\mu _s} = \\sqrt {n(n + 2)} BM$$\n\n$$ = \\sqrt {2(2 + 2)} = \\sqrt {2 \\times 4} = 2\\sqrt 2 = 2.84BM$$",
