      "s": "IIT-JEE 2006. Correct option: D. The step wise reaction between $\\mathrm{CuSO}_4$ and KCN is as given below :\n\nIn the first step, The $\\mathrm{CuSO}_4$ on addition of KCN loses its colour and produces copper (II) cyanide $\\mathrm{Cu}(\\mathrm{CN})_2$.\n\n$$ \\mathrm{CuSO}_4+2 \\mathrm{KCN} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Cu}(\\mathrm{CN})_2+\\mathrm{K}_2 \\mathrm{SO}_4 $$\n\nThe $\\mathrm{Cu}(\\mathrm{CN})_2$ formed is yellow coloured precipitate and unstable in nature.\n\nIn the step 2, the unstable $\\mathrm{Cu}(\\mathrm{CN})_2$ decomposes to white coloured precipitate of copper (I) cyanide as in reaction given below.\n\n$$ \\underset{\\text { yellow ppt }}{2 \\mathrm{Cu}(\\mathrm{CN})_2} \\longrightarrow \\underset{\\text { white ppt }}{2 \\mathrm{CuCN}}+(\\mathrm{CN})_2 $$\n\nOn addition of excess of potassium cyanide, colourless complex of tetracyanocuprate(I) is obtained.\n\n$$ \\begin{aligned} &\\mathrm{CuCN}+3 \\mathrm{KCN} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{~K}_3\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}(\\mathrm{CN})_4\\right]\\\\ &\\text { Potassium tetracyanocuprate (I) colourless } \\end{aligned} $$",
