      "s": "IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline. Correct option: D. $$ \\begin{aligned} & f(x)=e^{x^2}+e^{-x^2} \\\\\\\\ & \\begin{aligned} f^{\\prime}(x) & =e^{x^2} \\frac{d}{d x}\\left(x^2\\right)+e^{-x^2} \\frac{d}{d x}\\left(-x^2\\right) \\\\\\\\ & =e^{x^2}(2 x)+e^{-x^2}(-2 x) \\\\\\\\ & =2 x\\left(e^{x^2}-e^{-x^2}\\right) \\geq 0 \\forall x \\in[0,1] \\\\\\\\ g(x) & =x e^{x^2}+e^{-x^2} \\\\\\\\ h(x) & =x^2 e^{x^2}+e^{-x^2} \\end{aligned} \\end{aligned} $$\n\nClearly for $0 \\leq x \\leq 1 \\quad f(x) \\geq g(x) \\geq h(x)$\n\n$\\because f(1)=g(1)=h(1)=e+\\frac{1}{e}$ and $f(1)$ is greatest\n\n$$ \\because a=b=c=e+\\frac{1}{e} $$",
