      "q": "The total number of real solutions of the equation\n\n$ \\theta = \\tan^{-1}(2 \\tan \\theta) - \\frac{1}{2} \\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{6 \\tan \\theta}{9 + \\tan^2 \\theta}\\right) $\n\nis\n\n(Here, the inverse trigonometric functions $\\sin^{-1} x$ and $\\tan^{-1} x$ assume values in $[ -\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}]$ and $( -\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2})$, respectively.)",
      "qHtml": "<p>The total number of real solutions of the equation</p>\n<p>$ \\theta = \\tan^{-1}(2 \\tan \\theta) - \\frac{1}{2} \\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{6 \\tan \\theta}{9 + \\tan^2 \\theta}\\right) $</p>\n<p>is</p>\n<p>(Here, the inverse trigonometric functions $\\sin^{-1} x$ and $\\tan^{-1} x$ assume values in $[ -\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}]$ and $( -\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2})$, respectively.)</p>",
