      "s": "JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline. Correct option: C. Given, six cards and six envelops are numbered $$1,2,3,4,5$$ and 6.\n\nThe number of arrangements when all six\n\ncards are placed in wronge envelops\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n& =\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{6} \\,}} \\right.\\left(1-\\frac{1}{\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{1} \\,}} \\right.}+\\frac{1}{\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{2} \\,}} \\right.}-\\frac{1}{\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{3} \\,}} \\right.}+\\frac{1}{\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{4} \\,}} \\right.}-\\frac{1}{\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{5} \\,}} \\right.}+\\frac{1}{\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{6} \\,}} \\right.}\\right) \\\\\n& =\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{6} \\,}} \\right.\\left[1-\\frac{1}{1}+\\frac{3}{\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{3} \\,}} \\right.}-\\frac{1}{\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{3} \\,}} \\right.}+\\frac{5}{\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{5} \\,}} \\right.}-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{6} \\,}} \\right.}\\right] \\\\\n& =\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{6} \\,}} \\right.\\left[\\frac{2}{\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{3} \\,}} \\right.}+\\frac{4}{\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{5} \\,}} \\right.}+\\frac{1}{\\left| \\!{\\underline {\\,\n{6} \\,}} \\right.}\\right] \\\\\n& =2.6 .5 .4+4.6+1 \\\\\n& =240+24+1 \\\\\n& =265 \\\\\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIn the above dearrangement, there are 5 ways in which card number 1 is going wrong envelope i.e, other than envelope number 1. So, when card number 1 going in envelop number 2 is $$\\frac{265}{5}=53$$ ways.\n\nHint:\n\nIn the total dearrangement of 6 cards there are 5 ways in which card number 1 is going other than envelope number 1.",
