      "qHtml": "Let $X=\\left\\{(x, y) \\in \\mathbb{Z} \\times \\mathbb{Z}: \\frac{x^2}{8}+\\frac{y^2}{20}<1\\right.$ and $\\left.y^2<5 x\\right\\}$. Three distinct points $P, Q$ and $R$ are randomly chosen from $X$. Then the probability that $P, Q$ and $R$ form a triangle whose area is a positive integer, is :",
