      "s": "JEE Advanced 2024 Paper 1 Online. Correct option: C. [Diagram: JEE Advanced 2024 Paper 1 Online Mathematics - Circle Question 4 English Explanation]\n\nConsider centre as $$\\mathrm{P}(0, \\alpha), \\alpha>0$$\n\n$$\\left|\\frac{2(0)-\\alpha}{\\sqrt{5}}\\right|=\\mathrm{r}$$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n& |-\\alpha|=\\sqrt{5} r \\\\\n& \\alpha=\\sqrt{5} r \\\\\n& \\therefore \\alpha+r=5+\\sqrt{5} \\\\\n& \\sqrt{5} r+r=\\sqrt{5}(\\sqrt{5}+1) \\\\\n& r=\\sqrt{5}, \\alpha=5 \\\\\n& \\therefore P(0,5)\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFoot of perpendicular from $$P$$ to line $$2 x-y=0$$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{x-0}{2}=\\frac{y-5}{-1}=\\frac{-(2(0)-5)}{5}=1 \\\\\n& x=2, y=4 \\quad A_1(2,4)\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nLet $$\\mathrm{B}(\\mathrm{p}, \\mathrm{q}) \\quad \\therefore \\frac{\\mathrm{p}+2}{2}=0, \\frac{\\mathrm{q}+4}{2}=5$$\n\n$$\\therefore \\mathrm{p}=-2, \\mathrm{q}=6 \\quad B(-2,6)$$",
