      "s": "IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline. Correct option: C. Equation of circle C is\n\n$${(x + 3)^2} + {(y - 5)^2} = 9 + 25 - 30 = 4$$\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow {(x + 3)^2} + {(y - 5)^2} = {2^2}$$\n\nCentre = (3, $$-$$5)\n\nIf L 1 is diameter, then it passes through the center (3, $$-$$5),\n\n$$ \\therefore $$ $$2(3) + 3( - 5) + p - 3 = 0 \\Rightarrow p = 12$$\n\n$$\\therefore$$ L 1 is $$2x + 3y + 9 = 0$$\n\nand L 2 is $$2x + 3y + 15 = 0$$\n\nDistance of centre of circle from $${L_2}(d) = \\left| {{{2(3) + 3( - 5) + 15} \\over {\\sqrt {{2^2} + {3^2}} }}} \\right| = {6 \\over {\\sqrt {12} }} < 2$$ [radius of circle]\n\n$$\\therefore$$ L 2 is a chord of circle C.\n\nStatement 2 is false.\n\n[Diagram: IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline Mathematics - Circle Question 23 English Explanation]\n\nStatement - 1 is true. If L 1\nis a chord, L 2\nmay lie outside\nthe circle.",
