      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 2 Offline. Correct option: B. Given, PQ be a focal chord of the parabola $$y^2=4 a x$$\n\nLet $$\\mathrm{P}=\\left(a t^2, 2 a t\\right)$$ and $$\\mathrm{Q}\\left(\\frac{a}{t^2},-\\frac{2 a}{t}\\right)$$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 2 Offline Mathematics - Parabola Question 30 English Explanation]\n\nEquation of tangent at P is $$t y=x+a t^2\\quad \\text{... (i)}$$\n\nEquation of tangent at Q is $$-\\frac{y}{t}=x+\\frac{a}{t^2}\\quad \\text{... (ii)}$$\n\nLet $$R$$ is the point of intersection of tangents at $$P$$ and $$Q$$.\n\nOn solving Equation (i) and (ii)\n\n$$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{R}=\\left(-a, a\\left(t-\\frac{1}{t}\\right)\\right)$$\n\nGiven, the tangents of parabola $$y^2=4 a x$$ at P and $$Q$$ meet at a point lying on the line $$y=2 x +a$$.\n\n$$\\therefore \\mathrm{R}$$ must be lies on the line $$y=2 x+a$$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad a\\left(t-\\frac{1}{t}\\right)=-2 a+a \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad t-\\frac{1}{t}=-1 \\quad \\text{... (iii)}\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nLet the length of chord PQ is L\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{L}=\\sqrt{\\left(a t^2-\\frac{a}{t^2}\\right)^2+\\left(2 a t+\\frac{2 a}{t}\\right)^2} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{L}=a \\sqrt{\\left(t-\\frac{1}{t}\\right)^2\\left(t+\\frac{1}{t}\\right)^2+4\\left(t+\\frac{1}{t}\\right)^2} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{L}=a \\sqrt{\\left(t-\\frac{1}{t}\\right)^2\\left(\\left(t-\\frac{1}{t}\\right)^2+4\\right)+4\\left(\\left(t-\\frac{1}{t}\\right)^2+4\\right)} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{L}=a \\sqrt{1 \\cdot(1+4)+4 \\cdot(1+4)} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{L}=5 a\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nHints:\n\nIf $$P Q$$ is a focal chord of parabola $$y^2=4 a x$$, then $$\\mathrm{P}=\\left(a t^2, 2 a t\\right)$$ and $$\\mathrm{Q}=\\left(\\frac{a}{t^2}, \\frac{-2 a}{t}\\right)$$",
