      "q": "Let the straight line $y=2 x$ touch a circle with center $(0, \\alpha), \\alpha>0$, and radius $r$ at a point $A_1$. Let $B_1$ be the point on the circle such that the line segment $A_1 B_1$ is a diameter of the circle. Let $\\alpha+r=5+\\sqrt{5}$.\n\nMatch each entry in List-I to the correct entry in List-II .\n\nList-I\nList-II\n\n(P) $\\alpha$ equals\n(1) $(-2, 4)$\n\n(Q) $r$ equals\n(2) $\\sqrt{5}$\n\n(R) $A_1$ equals\n(3) $(-2, 6)$\n\n(S) $B_1$ equals\n(4) $5$\n\n(5) $(2, 4)$\n\nThe correct option is",
      "qHtml": "<p>Let the straight line $y=2 x$ touch a circle with center $(0, \\alpha), \\alpha>0$, and radius $r$ at a point $A_1$. Let $B_1$ be the point on the circle such that the line segment $A_1 B_1$ is a diameter of the circle. Let $\\alpha+r=5+\\sqrt{5}$.</p>\n\n<p>Match each entry in <b>List-I</b> to the correct entry in <b>List-II</b>.\n</p>\n\n<table>\n    <thead>\n        <tr>\n            <th>List-I</th>\n            <th>List-II</th>\n        </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n        <tr>\n            <td>(P) $\\alpha$ equals</td>\n            <td>(1) $(-2, 4)$</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td>(Q) $r$ equals</td>\n            <td>(2) $\\sqrt{5}$</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td>(R) $A_1$ equals</td>\n            <td>(3) $(-2, 6)$</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td>(S) $B_1$ equals</td>\n            <td>(4) $5$</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td></td>\n            <td>(5) $(2, 4)$</td>\n        </tr>\n    </tbody>\n</table>\n\n\n<br>The correct option is",
