      "q": "Let $ \\vec{a}, \\vec{b} $ be two vectors, and let P, Q and R be the points with position vectors $ \\vec{a}, \\vec{b} $ and $ \\vec{a} + \\vec{b} $ , respectively, with respect to the origin O . If $ |\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}| = \\sqrt{21} $ , $ |\\vec{a} - \\vec{b}| = 3 $ , and $ \\vec{a} $ and $ (\\vec{a} - \\vec{b}) $ are perpendicular to each other, then the area of the triangle OPR is :",
