      "s": "JEE Advanced 2023 Paper 2 Online. Correct option: B. $\\begin{aligned} & P(\\vec{a})=\\hat{i}+2 \\hat{j}-5 \\hat{k} \\\\\\\\ & Q(\\vec{b})=3 \\hat{i}+6 \\hat{j}+3 \\hat{k} \\\\\\\\ & R(\\vec{c})=\\frac{17}{5} \\hat{i}+\\frac{16}{5} \\hat{j}+7 \\hat{k} \\\\\\\\ & S(\\vec{d})=2 \\hat{i}+\\hat{j}+\\hat{k}\\end{aligned}$\n\nFrom option\n(A) :\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2023 Paper 2 Online Mathematics - Vector Algebra Question 10 English Explanation 1]\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& {[\\overrightarrow{P Q}, \\overrightarrow{P R}, \\overrightarrow{P S}] \\rightarrow \\text { S.T.P }} \\\\\\\\\n& \\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}\n2 & 4 & 6 \\\\\n\\frac{12}{5} & \\frac{6}{5} & 12 \\\\\n1 & -1 & 6\n\\end{array}\\right|=0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence P, Q, R, S are coplanar.\n\nFrom option\n(B) :\n\n$\\frac{\\vec{b}+2 \\vec{d}}{3}=\\frac{7 i+8 j+5 k}{3}$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Advanced 2023 Paper 2 Online Mathematics - Vector Algebra Question 10 English Explanation 2]\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\frac{17 \\lambda}{5}+1}{1+\\lambda}=\\frac{7}{3} \\\\\\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{(17 \\lambda+5)}{1+\\lambda}=\\frac{35}{3} \\\\\\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 15 \\lambda+15=35+35 \\lambda \\\\\\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 16 \\lambda=20 \\\\\\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\lambda=\\frac{5}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence option (B) is correct.\n\n(D)\n\n$\\quad \\begin{aligned}|\\vec{b} \\times \\vec{d}|^2 & =|\\vec{b}|^2|\\vec{d}|^2-(\\vec{b} \\cdot \\vec{d})^2 \\\\\\\\ & =54 \\times 6-225 \\\\\\\\ & =324-225 \\\\\\\\ & =99\\end{aligned}$",
