      "q": "Let $f:(0,1) \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ be the function defined as $f(x)=\\sqrt{n}$ if $x \\in\\left[\\frac{1}{n+1}, \\frac{1}{n}\\right)$ where $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$. Let $g:(0,1) \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ be a function such that $\\int\\limits_{x^2}^x \\sqrt{\\frac{1-t}{t}} d t < g(x) < 2 \\sqrt{x}$ for all $x \\in(0,1)$.\nThen $\\lim\\limits_{x \\rightarrow 0} f(x) g(x)$",
      "qHtml": "Let $f:(0,1) \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ be the function defined as $f(x)=\\sqrt{n}$ if $x \\in\\left[\\frac{1}{n+1}, \\frac{1}{n}\\right)$ where $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$. Let $g:(0,1) \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ be a function such that $\\int\\limits_{x^2}^x \\sqrt{\\frac{1-t}{t}} d t < g(x) < 2 \\sqrt{x}$ for all $x \\in(0,1)$. \nThen $\\lim\\limits_{x \\rightarrow 0} f(x) g(x)$",
